abel)\n                  extra-schemes)))\n\n\n(defn parse-arg\n  \"The `--index-store` value as a spec: `:mem`, or `{:type :file :dir dir}`\n   for `file:<dir>`.  A missing value, an unknown scheme, and an empty\n   directory are refused here — with the supported forms named — so the\n   arguments parser can refuse a bad flag before anything composes.\n\n   `extra-schemes` registers the schemes a storage composition adds, each\n   `{:prefix \\\"<scheme>:\\\" :label \\\"<as documented>\\\" :parse (fn [dir]\n   spec)}`.  They are plain data: this namespace matches a prefix and\n   calls `:parse` with the directory, and never learns what the answer\n   means.  A composition's own checked spec then validates it\n   (`checked-spec` refuses a type it does not know, so a registered\n   scheme whose spec reaches the engine unchecked is still refused).\"\n  ([value] (parse-arg value nil))\n  ([value extra-schemes]\n   (let [supported (supported-text extra-schemes)\n         extra (when (string? value)\n                 (some (fn [{:keys [prefix parse]}]\n                         (when (str/starts-with? value prefix)\n                           (let [dir (subs value (count prefix))]\n                             (if (str/blank? dir)\n                               (throw (ex-info (str \"--index-store \" prefix\n                                                    \"<dir> needs a directory\")\n                                               {:value value\n                                                :supported supported}))\n                               (parse dir)))))\n                       extra-schemes))]\n     (cond\n       (nil? value)\n       (throw (ex-info (str \"--index-store needs a value: \" supported)\n                       {:value value\n                        :supported supported}))\n\n       (some? extra)\n       extra\n\n       (= value \"mem\")\n       :mem\n\n       (str/starts-with? value file-scheme)\n       (let [dir (subs value (count file-scheme))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:22:   flag on closures and no expansion ledger. Expansion is a process on the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:4:   A process between two media: it observes `program-in` batches\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:54:since the J7 slices 1-2 (2026-11-15; the sections 6-7 process/interop gate of\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:202:- **Refusals & Locking:** Clashing flags (e.g., saved `--dht-*` flags with `--index-store mem`) refuse startup and name `--reset`. Give each process its own `--name` or `--dir`. ClojureDart has no home directory, so pass `--dir` explicitly to save state.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:255:- **Operational notes:** Keep key files outside `/tmp` and never delete a node's directory. Closing a node discards its unacknowledged retry queue. For Node process tests (`test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj`), build `target/yin-repl.js` with `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/front.cljc:4:   outside its process (UCF 7.7.8, 7.9; docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:750:         ;; processed exactly once; every reference resolves to the same\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/bytecode-vm-optimization.md:544:CLJD directly in the Flutter process is the better path:\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:760: :val <ast-node>      ; The node that provides the value to \"send\" to the resumed process\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:979:> (decision 1 of `yin.vm.macro.md`)... Expansion is a process on the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:1002:The `:dao.stream.apply/call` node represents a cross-process FFI call: it\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:1005:calling a Clojure function directly in-process.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc:177:   :dao.stream.journal/failure-model :process-crash|:power-loss|:none\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc:186:  {:none 0 :process-crash 1 :power-loss 2})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc:191:   requires surviving `required`, :process-crash or :power-loss: its\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority.