{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,95p' src/jolt/dao/host/hash.jolt; sed -n '1,100p' src/jolt/dao/host/sign.jolt; sed -n '1,100p' src/jolt/yin/vm/linker/random.jolt; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(def(n|macro).*' src/z* src/dev/jolt_diag 2>/dev/null | head -75\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.host.hash\n  \"The jolt override of src/cljc/dao/host/hash.cljc (the :jolt alias puts\n   src/jolt first, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.2, §6.2,\n   §6.3): the same public entries, arities, docstrings and refusal data\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, table A).\n\n   P entries (§2.4): `blake3-bytes` and `sha256-bytes`. They take host\n   bytes (jolt's byte array) and return fresh host bytes representing the\n   32-byte digest (256 bits). They leave their arguments unmodified.\n\n   Both are `:blocking` calls into native/jolt-crypto, which `bb\n   build:jolt-native` builds: BLAKE3 is the vendored upstream C reference,\n   SHA-256 the declared system libcrypto's EVP API. The input is copied into\n   caller-owned native memory (never a C string, so embedded NUL is data),\n   the digest is read back into a fresh jolt byte array, and the memory is\n   freed on every path: each native acquisition owns its own release,\n   established as soon as it is acquired (`with-native`), so a later\n   allocation or copy that fails still frees every earlier buffer, and each\n   free runs whether or not another failed.\n\n   Loading this namespace is the provenance gate (§6.3): it refuses, by\n   throwing, unless the wrapper writes this namespace's layout and reports\n   that every EVP entry resolved to exactly the library jolt-toolchain.edn\n   qualified for this platform (:native :libcrypto :qualified): the same\n   canonical real path (which the declared :path must also resolve to), the\n   same OpenSSL_version_num and the same file SHA-256, at no lower than\n   :min-version. An upgrade, a repointed link or a replaced file therefore\n   fails until requalified (the procedure is in jolt-toolchain.edn). No\n   digest is computed before that check passes; a missing library fails the\n   load.\n\n   String digesting is a table B portable composition over `dao.host.text`\n   and these byte primitives (`blake3`, `sha256`, `digest-string`,\n   `digest-bytes`), hosted in `dao.jing`.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The native library and its provenance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private platform\n  ;; as yang.antlr.cst decides it: jolt's os.name/os.arch shim can answer\n  ;; nil, which reads as Linux and x86_64\n  (let [os (str/lower-case (or (System/getProperty \"os.name\") \"\"))\n        arch (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")]\n    (str (if (str/includes? os \"mac\") \"darwin\" \"linux\") \"-\"\n         (if (#{\"aarch64\" \"arm64\"} arch) \"arm64\" \"x86_64\"))))\n\n\n(def ^:private library\n  ;; the wrapper `bb build:jolt-native` builds, under the working directory\n  (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\") \"/build/native/\" platform\n       \"/jolt-crypto/lib/libjolt_crypto\"\n       (if (str/starts-with? platform \"darwin\") \".dylib\" \".so\")))\n\n\n(def ^:private libcrypto-declaration\n  (get-in (edn/read-string (slurp (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\")\n                                       \"/jolt-toolchain.edn\")))\n          [:native :libcrypto]))\n\n\n(ffi/load-library library)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-layout-version \"jolt_crypto_layout_version\" [] :int)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-provenance \"jolt_crypto_provenance\" [:pointer :size_t] :int)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-blake3 \"jolt_crypto_blake3\"\n            [:pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-sha256 \"jolt_crypto_sha256\"\n            [:pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n\n\n;; 3 (J2): the random entry joined the exported set (jolt_crypto_random for\n;; yin.vm.linker.sign/generate's :jolt arm); a J1b-built wrapper answers 2 and\n;; is refused here rather than at a missing-symbol error in the linker.\n;; 4 (J6c): jolt_crypto_sha1 joined it (dao.stream.ws.crypto) and EVP_sha1\n;; the provenance audit; a J2-built wrapper answers 3 and is refused here.\n(def ^:private layout 4)\n\n\n(defn- refuse-load\n  [message data]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"jolt-crypto refused: \" message)\n                  (assoc data :library library))))\n\n\n(when-not (= layout (c-layout-version))\n(ns dao.host.sign\n  \"The jolt override of src/cljc/dao/host/sign.cljc (the :jolt alias puts\n   src/jolt first, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.2, §6.3):\n   the same public entries, arities, docstrings and refusal data\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, table A).\n\n   P entries (§2.4):\n   - `keypair-from-seed`: takes 32-byte seed (host bytes), returns\n     `{:seed <32 bytes>, :public <32 bytes>}` as fresh host bytes.\n   - `sign`: takes 32-byte seed and arbitrary message (host bytes),\n     returns 64-byte Ed25519 signature as fresh host bytes.\n   - `verify`: takes 32-byte public key, arbitrary message, and 64-byte signature\n     (all host bytes), returns boolean (true if valid, false otherwise).\n\n   Deterministic seed replay through the declared system libcrypto's raw\n   Ed25519 keys (EVP_PKEY_new_raw_private_key, one-shot EVP_DigestSign and\n   EVP_DigestVerify), behind native/jolt-crypto. The library and its\n   provenance gate are dao.host.hash's: requiring it first means no key is\n   used before that check passes.\n\n   Each native acquisition owns its own release, established as soon as it\n   is acquired, so a later allocation or copy that fails still releases\n   every earlier buffer, and each release runs whether or not another\n   failed. Native memory that held seed bytes is zeroed by the wrapper's\n   jolt_crypto_cleanse (OPENSSL_cleanse, which allocates nothing) before it\n   is freed, on every path, including a seed copy that failed part way.\n   Fresh entropy key generation (`generate`) is deferred (§9.1) and remains\n   in `yin.vm.linker.sign`.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    ;; loaded for its provenance gate, which must pass before any call here\n    [dao.host.hash]\n    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\n\n\n(def ^:private library\n  ;; the same wrapper dao.host.hash loaded and qualified (jolt's os.name and\n  ;; os.arch shim can answer nil, which reads as Linux and x86_64)\n  (let [os (str/lower-case (or (System/getProperty \"os.name\") \"\"))\n        arch (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")\n        darwin? (str/includes? os \"mac\")]\n    (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\") \"/build/native/\"\n         (if darwin? \"darwin\" \"linux\") \"-\"\n         (if (#{\"aarch64\" \"arm64\"} arch) \"arm64\" \"x86_64\")\n         \"/jolt-crypto/lib/libjolt_crypto\" (if darwin? \".dylib\" \".so\"))))\n\n\n(ffi/load-library library)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-public \"jolt_crypto_ed25519_public\"\n  [:pointer :pointer] :int :blocking)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-sign \"jolt_crypto_ed25519_sign\"\n  [:pointer :pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-verify \"jolt_crypto_ed25519_verify\"\n  [:pointer :pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-cleanse \"jolt_crypto_cleanse\" [:pointer :size_t] :void)\n\n\n(defn- check-bytes!\n  [entry name-kw bs expected-len]\n  (when-not (bytes/bytes? bs)\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.host refused: \" entry \" unsupported-value (expected \" (name name-kw) \" host bytes)\")\n                    {:dao.host/refusal :unsupported-value\n                     :dao.host/entry entry\n                     :target name-kw})))\n  (when (and expected-len (not= (bytes/length bs) expected-len))\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.host refused: \" entry \" out-of-range (expected \" expected-len \" bytes, got \" (bytes/length bs) \")\")\n                    {:dao.host/refusal :out-of-range\n                     :dao.host/entry entry\n                     :expected expected-len\n                     :actual (bytes/length bs)}))))\n\n\n(defn- acquire\n  \"Caller-owned native memory of `n` bytes (at least one); throws when the\n   allocator answers NULL, so a caller never holds an unowned pointer.\"\n  [n]\n  (let [p (ffi/alloc (max 1 n))]\n    (when (ffi/null? p)\n      (throw (ex-info \"jolt-crypto native allocation failed\" {:bytes n})))\n    p))\n\n\n(defn- with-native\n  \"(f p) over `n` bytes of native memory, freed however `f` exits.\"\n  [n f]\n  (let [p (acquire n)]\n    (try (f p) (finally (ffi/free p)))))\n\n\n(defn- with-copy\n  \"(f p) over a native copy of `bs`, freed however the copy or `f` exits.\"\n  [bs f]\n  (let [n (alength bs)]\n    (with-native n\n      (fn [p]\n        (when (pos? n) (ffi/write-array p bs))\n        (f p)))))\n\n\n(ns yin.vm.linker.random\n  \"The jolt-only fresh-entropy adapter behind `yin.vm.linker.sign/generate`'s\n   `:jolt` arm, delegating to `dao.posix.random/rand-bytes`.\"\n  (:require [dao.posix.random :as posix.random]))\n\n\n(defn rand-bytes\n  \"Delegates to `dao.posix.random/rand-bytes`.\"\n  [n]\n  (posix.random/rand-bytes n))\nzsh:1: no matches found: src/z*\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
