{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '88,218p' host/chez/converters.ss; sed -n '1,110p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; tail -30 /private/tmp/jolt-p1c-probe2.log; tail -8 /private/tmp/jolt-p1c-baseline.log; ls -l /private/tmp/jolt-p1c-native\"","aggregated_output":"      (jolt-masked-after lv (set-virtual-register! jolt-vreg-print-readably prev)))))\n(def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"__print1\" jolt-print-one)\n\n;; str: a top-level string/scalar renders as jolt-str-render-one (raw string,\n;; \"Infinity\"…), but a COLLECTION renders as its readable form — nested strings\n;; are QUOTED ((str [\"x\"]) => \"[\\\"x\\\"]\"), matching the JVM (a collection's\n;; toString is readable). jolt-pr-readable resolves at call time.\n;; A host type whose own toString must win over the rendering below — set by\n;; records.ss for a deftype/record that declares one. Returns the string, or #f to\n;; fall through. Kept as one hook rather than a registry arm because the arms are\n;; only reached for values no branch here claims, and a record is claimed.\n(define str-tostring-hook #f)\n(define (set-str-tostring-hook! f) (set! str-tostring-hook f))\n(define (jolt-str-one v)\n  (let ((own (and str-tostring-hook (str-tostring-hook v))))\n    (cond\n      ((string? own) own)\n      ((or (pvec? v) (pmap? v) (pset? v) (cseq? v) (empty-list-t? v) (jolt-lazyseq? v))\n       (jolt-pr-readable v))\n      (else (jolt-str-render-one v)))))\n;; A string renders as itself. jolt-str-one asks the toString hook first, but\n;; that hook only ever answers for a record (protocols.ss), so a string can skip\n;; it and the type cond behind it: strings are most of what str is handed.\n(define (jolt-str-piece v) (if (string? v) v (jolt-str-one v)))\n;; Fixed entries for two and three arguments — the arities library code\n;; actually writes — build the result in one string-append with no rest list,\n;; no accumulator and no reverse. The variadic entry keeps its shape. Measured\n;; 56 ns against string-append's 1 ns for (str s \"!\") before this.\n;; Is X a surrogate unit (values.ss jsurr)? A string, nearly every str argument,\n;; answers with one inline type test.\n(define-syntax str-unit?\n  (syntax-rules () ((_ x) (let ((v x)) (and (not (string? v)) (jsurr? v))))))\n(define jolt-str\n  (case-lambda\n    (() \"\")\n    ;; single arg returns its rendering directly (no string-append copy), so\n    ;; (str sym) hands back the symbol's own name string — JVM (str x) is\n    ;; x.toString(), and core.logic's non-unique lvar equality compares those by\n    ;; identity.\n    ((a) (jolt-str-one a))                ; a lone unit renders U+FFFD itself\n    ;; A surrogate unit argument (a (char 0xD83D)) joins with the one after it:\n    ;; only a unit can start a pair, so the test is on every argument but the\n    ;; last, behind string? so a string argument pays one inline type test.\n    ((a b) (if (str-unit? a)\n               (jolt-str-units (list a b))\n               (string-append (jolt-str-piece a) (jolt-str-piece b))))\n    ((a b c) (if (or (str-unit? a) (str-unit? b))\n                 (jolt-str-units (list a b c))\n                 (string-append (jolt-str-piece a) (jolt-str-piece b) (jolt-str-piece c))))\n    ((a b c . rest)\n     (if (or (str-unit? a) (str-unit? b) (str-unit? c))\n         (jolt-str-units (cons a (cons b (cons c rest))))\n         (let loop ((xs rest) (acc (list (jolt-str-piece c) (jolt-str-piece b) (jolt-str-piece a))))\n           (cond\n             ((null? xs) (apply string-append (reverse acc)))\n             ((str-unit? (car xs)) (jolt-str-units (cons a (cons b (cons c rest)))))\n             (else (loop (cdr xs) (cons (jolt-str-piece (car xs)) acc)))))))))\n;; str over arguments among which are surrogate units: a high unit directly\n;; followed by a low one is the astral character they spell; any other unit is\n;; U+FFFD (its str-render, surrogates.ss), since a jolt string holds code points.\n(define (jolt-str-units xs)\n  (let loop ((xs xs) (acc '()))\n    (cond\n      ((null? xs) (apply string-append (reverse acc)))\n      ((and (jsurr-high? (car xs)) (pair? (cdr xs)) (jsurr-low? (cadr xs)))\n       (loop (cddr xs)\n             (cons (string (surrogates->char (jsurr-unit (car xs)) (jsurr-unit (cadr xs)))) acc)))\n      (else (loop (cdr xs) (cons (jolt-str-piece (car xs)) acc))))))\n\n;; jolt indices are flonums; substring etc. need exact ints. A fixnum is already\n;; one — this sits on the proven-string .charAt/.substring path, so it must not\n;; call anything for the common case.\n(define (jolt->idx n) (if (fixnum? n) n (exact (truncate (jolt-need-num n)))))\n;; String.charAt and every CharSequence charAt over a string's characters\n;; (StringBuilder reads its buffer through the same check): an index outside\n;; [0, length) is the JVM's StringIndexOutOfBoundsException with its message,\n;; not Chez's string-ref error.\n(define (char-index-oob i n)\n  (index-int-check! i)                  ; an int parameter: RT.intCast first\n  (throw-jvm 'StringIndexOutOfBoundsException\n             (string-append \"Index \" (number->string i) \" out of bounds for length \"\n                            (number->string n))))\n\n(define (jolt-char-at s i)\n  (let ((i (jolt->idx i)))\n    (if (and (fixnum? i) (fx>=? i 0) (fx<? i (string-length s)))\n        (string-ref s i)\n        (char-index-oob i (string-length s)))))\n\n;; Chez's `substring` walks the span a character at a time; allocating the result\n;; and asking for the block move is ~3.7x faster for the spans a parser, a reader\n;; or a splitter cuts. Measured on Chez 10.4.1 / x86_64, 2048 chars out of 4300:\n;; `substring` 4.27us, `(make-string n)` + `string-copy!` 1.17us — and the\n;; make-string alone is 1.29us of that, so the copy itself is free and what the\n;; primitive spends is the per-character loop. Out-of-range falls through to\n;; `substring` so the range error stays the one host-faults.ss classifies. The\n;; copy goes through the adapter's sa-string-copy-range! rather than a raw\n;; string-copy!: this file is shared with the Gambit host, whose R7RS\n;; string-copy! takes the same five arguments in the opposite direction.\n(define (jolt-substr s start end)\n  (if (and (fixnum? start) (fixnum? end)\n           (fx>=? start 0) (fx<=? start end) (fx<=? end (string-length s)))\n      (let ((d (make-string (fx- end start))))\n        (sa-string-copy-range! d 0 s start end)\n        d)\n      (begin (index-int-check! start) (index-int-check! end) (substring s start end))))\n\n;; clojure.string/escape. Invoke cmap once per character, but keep each run\n;; of unchanged text as one piece. Joining the raw replacements with str's\n;; renderer also lets adjacent surrogate Character values form a pair.\n(define (str-escape-by input cmap)\n  (let* ((s (jolt-need-string input)) (n (string-length s)))\n    (define (save-span start end pieces)\n      (if (fx=? start end) pieces (cons (substring s start end) pieces)))\n    (let loop ((i 0) (start 0) (pieces '()))\n      (if (fx=? i n)\n          (if (null? pieces)\n              (string-copy s)\n              (let ((parts (reverse (save-span start n pieces))))\n                (if (for-all string? parts) (apply string-append parts) (jolt-str-units parts))))\n          (let ((rep (jolt-invoke1 cmap (string-ref s i))) (next (fx+ i 1)))\n            (if (jolt-truthy? rep)\n                (loop next next (cons rep (save-span start i pieces)))\n                (loop next start pieces)))))))\n(def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"__str-escape-by\" str-escape-by)\n\n;; case-lambda, not `. end`: a rest-arg list allocated on every call is most of\n;; what a one-character (subs txt i (inc i)) costs, and a parser does that per\n;; input position.\n(define jolt-subs\n  (case-lambda\n;; host-ffi.ss — the jolt.ffi host-owned surface for the GAMBIT target\n;; (P1b-stage1). On Chez these vars live in host/chez/java/ffi.ss, which the\n;; gambit boot manifest excludes — without this file every jolt.ffi name was an\n;; unbound global (the same shape the host-vars.ss degradation fixed for\n;; clojure.core). Stage-1 binds the memory/loader/errno surface the qualified\n;; tier backs (the adapter rows + the native bridge), implements what the\n;; stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj public functions call into, and binds EVERYTHING ELSE to\n;; a message-carrying refusal — nothing stays unbound, nothing pretends.\n;;\n;; Loaded after host-vars.ss, before the seed image (same rule: these bindings\n;; are the last word for the names the excluded ffi.ss owned). Requires the\n;; booted kernel (jolt-nil, def-var!, jolt-hash-map, make-pvec, ...) — this\n;; file is boot-world only; the sa-* tier it leans on also loads standalone\n;; under gambitcheck without it.\n\n(define (joltffi-public-error thunk)\n  (guard (e (#t (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException\n                            (or (condition-message e) \"jolt.ffi: native bridge failure\"))))\n    (thunk)))\n\n(define (joltffi-public-blocking-raise)\n  (joltffi-public-error sa-foreign-procedure-blocking-raise))\n\n(define (joltffi-public-procedure args ret name variadic capture?)\n  (let ((fp (joltffi-public-error\n             (lambda () ((if capture? joltffi-foreign-capture-procedure joltffi-foreign-procedure)\n                         args ret name variadic)))))\n    (lambda args\n      (joltffi-public-error (lambda () (apply fp args))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-str-arg what x)\n  (if (jolt-nil? x)\n      (throw-jvm 'IllegalArgumentException\n                 (string-append \"jolt.ffi: \" what \" must be a string, got nil\"))\n      (jolt-str-render-one x)))\n\n;; ---- emitted-text helpers the compiler's ordinary-call wrappers lean on -----\n;; The :string conversions invert per direction like the Chez pair; jolt truthy\n;; rule for :bool; jfloat unboxing for :float/:double. jolt-ffi-c->string maps\n;; the adapter's NULL-string #f to jolt-nil (values.ss's sentinel — bound by\n;; the time any of these RUN; the define only closes over it).\n(define (jolt-ffi-string->c x)\n  (cond ((string? x) x)\n        ((jolt-nil? x) #f)                ; nil IS NULL, in both directions\n        (else (throw-jvm 'IllegalArgumentException\n                         (string-append \"jolt.ffi: :string got \" (jolt-pr-str x)\n                                        \" — NULL is spelled nil\")))))\n(define (jolt-ffi-c->string x) (if x x jolt-nil))\n(define (jolt-ffi-bool->c v) (if (or (jolt-nil? v) (eq? v #f)) 0 1))\n(define (jolt-ffi-c->bool raw) (not (eqv? (jnum->exact raw) 0)))\n(define (jolt-ffi-float->c x) (if (jfloat? x) (jfloat-fl x) x))\n\n;; A :string ARGUMENT travels as u8* on Chez (an immobile copy). Gambit has no\n;; immobile allocation and the stage-1 bridge carries no :string-argument shape\n;; (the registry has none), so this raises BEFORE the unbound-identifier fate\n;; the pre-stage1 boot would have dealt: the adapter's shape validation refuses\n;; :string arguments, and this helper — which the emitted wrapper evaluates\n;; first — refuses for any path that might reach it out of order.\n(define (jolt-ffi-string-arg x)\n  (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException\n             \"jolt.ffi: :string arguments are unsupported on the gambit target — no immobile allocation behind the stage-1 bridge\"))\n\n;; The emitted call keeps string copies live until C returns; identity here,\n;; because nothing that evaluates it can have a live foreign reference (the\n;; string-arg path above refuses first). Bound so the emitted TEXT never dies\n;; on an unbound identifier at load.\n(define (keep-live x) x)\n\n;; jolt-ffi-function-pointer: the pointer-call null guard (backend\n;; ffi-pointer-procedure-expr emits it ahead of each call). Pointer-call\n;; bindings are compile-time-refused on :gambit, so this only guards paths that\n;; hand a raw address to the ordinary tier.\n(define (jolt-ffi-function-pointer ptr)\n  (let ((address (if (jolt-nil? ptr) 0 (jnum->exact ptr))))\n    (if (eqv? address 0)\n        (throw-jvm 'NullPointerException \"jolt.ffi: null C function pointer\")\n        address)))\n\n;; jolt-ffi-dlsym-native (the compiler's emitted scoped probe) is defined in\n;; the adapter itself — it must exist in every world the emitted text loads in,\n;; including the adapter-only gambitcheck unit.\n\n;; ---- foreign memory over the adapter tier -------------------------------------\n;; alloc returns the ADDRESS (an exact integer); read/write take the type\n;; keyword and the offset LAST (the babashka.ffi order the stdlib wrapper\n;; keeps). Type keywords arrive as jolt keywords; the stdlib resolves layouts\n;; and places before calling, so these see scalars only.\n(define (joltffi-keyword-name kw)\n  (if (keyword-t? kw) (keyword-t-name kw) (joltffi-str-arg \"foreign type\" kw)))\n\n(define (joltffi-type->chez kw)\n  (let ((n (joltffi-keyword-name kw)))\n    (cond\n      ((string=? n \"int\") 'int)\n      ((string=? n \"uint\") 'unsigned-int)\n      ((or (string=? n \"int8\") (string=? n \"i8\")) 'integer-8)\n      ((or (string=? n \"uint8\") (string=? n \"u8\") (string=? n \"byte\")) 'unsigned-8)\n      ((or (string=? n \"int16\") (string=? n \"short\")) 'integer-16)\n      ((or (string=? n \"uint16\") (string=? n \"ushort\")) 'unsigned-16)\n      ((string=? n \"int32\") 'integer-32)\n      ((string=? n \"uint32\") 'unsigned-32)\n      ((string=? n \"long\") 'long)\n      ((string=? n \"ulong\") 'unsigned-long)\n      ((string=? n \"int64\") 'integer-64)\n      ((string=? n \"uint64\") 'unsigned-64)\n      ((string=? n \"size_t\") 'size_t)\n      ((string=? n \"ssize_t\") 'ssize_t)\n      ((string=? n \"iptr\") 'iptr)\n      ((string=? n \"uptr\") 'uptr)\n      ((string=? n \"double\") 'double)\nloading yin.repl.main /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\nloading yin.repl.host.common /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/host/common.cljc\nloading clojure.string stdlib/clojure/string.clj\nloading dao.stream.waitset.cadence /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/waitset/cadence.cljc\nhost/gambit/ffi/record-toolchain.sh: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/verify-toolchain.sh: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/verify-digests.sh: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh: OK\ngambitffi: platform=darwin-arm64 manifest=/Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p1c/build/gambit-ffi/provenance/TOOLCHAIN.darwin-arm64.json\ngambitffi: local toolchain provenance verified (7 inputs)\ncp host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm host/gambit/ffi/generated-shims.scm build/gambit-ffi/\ncd build/gambit-ffi && sh ../../host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 120 /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/bin/gsc -dynamic -keep-temp joltffi-bridge.scm\ntotal 8\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 sto  wheel  68 Nov 20 00:14 boot.ss\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 sto  wheel   0 Nov 20 00:14 compile.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
