{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_98","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > /private/tmp/jolt-p1c-findings-body.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Implementation and qualification\n\n- Native Gambit source loading is opt-in. The launcher puts the companion checkout's Jolt shadows before its portable roots and uses Jolt's existing \"'`require` seam and Gambit compiler (`host/gambit/yin-repl-main.ss:24–41`, `host/gambit/source-loader.ss:19–69`). It opens the qualified bridge from the Jolt checkout before moving the working directory to datomworld. Loaded namespaces, cycles and failed loads have distinct states. `:as-alias` cannot satisfy a subsequent ordinary `require` by itself.\n- Large source strings compile on this path. The emitter'\"'s \"'`apply str` over a namespace docstring exhausted a Gambit argument frame. The Gambit streaming path preserves rendering and surrogate-pair handling (`host/gambit/host-apply.ss:1–29`). `gambitsourceload` exercised a real `.cljc`/`.jolt` dependency pair, alias resolution, caller namespace, reload and missing-source refusals, paired surrogates, and a 9,000-character source literal (`host/gambit/source-loader-test.ss:13–28`). Gambit'\"'s array predicates report false while its Jolt array constructors continue to refuse (\"'`host/gambit/host-vars.ss:238–246`, `:391–397`).\n- `make gambityinrepl` is an opt-in acceptance attempt against the external checkout. It feeds the real entry point, caps runtime at 240 seconds, and requires ordered prompt replies for arithmetic, a lambda, a definition used on the next line, language refusal, an FFI result, further evaluation and `Bye` (`Makefile`, `test/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh:10–46`). A zero-exit control returning three replies was rejected. The gate remains outside the existing `gambitffi` aggregate while the Yin path is red.\n\n## What remains blocked\n\nThe native attempt reaches the startup closure but never reaches a `yin>` prompt. The exact diagnostic is below. Two initial blockers were independently isolated. Stock Gambit first exhausted an argument frame while compiling the `jolt.ffi` namespace documentation. With that path repaired or bypassed for diagnosis, the closure encountered the missing array predicates `clojure.core/bytes?` (`src/jolt/dao/host/bytes.jolt:24–28`) and `array?` (`stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj:1117`). The committed fixes allow the predicates to compile. Actual Jolt byte storage, required by the existing DaoJing byte and CBOR adapters, still needs Gambit host wiring.\n\nA static :jolt/:clj `ns`-declaration traversal using the Jolt shadow order reached 164 namespaces. That count describes the require closure. The local default path constructs a DaoJing index store (`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1173–1184`, `src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc`), and DaoJing loads the hash adapter (`src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:26–34`, `:91–94`). The Jolt hash adapter eagerly loads its native library and declares BLAKE3 and SHA-256 as `:blocking` (`src/jolt/dao/host/hash.jolt:62–78`, `:189–200`). The component probe below verified the exact BLAKE3 declaration'\"'s refusal. The existing terminal owner also expects Jolt's native waitset and WebSocket adapter (\"'`src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:1218–1250`). Python requires the native parser'\"'s blocking export (\"'`src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:60–74`). A full local session needs Gambit-backed host implementations for the required storage and terminal seams, plus explicit admission of the bounded `jolt.ffi` module into the Yin VM. The direct Jolt FFI result below leaves that guest-module work open.\n\nThe original user objective is partial. Jolt source/eval and the stage‑1 FFI tier run under native Gambit 4.9.8 on macOS arm64. `yin.repl` has not started there. The component probes demonstrate the existing subprocess, FASL, native compilation and blocking FFI refusals. Inline Yin refusal and continuation, a native Yin frontend result, and FFI through a Yin guest expression remain unverified. C4'\"'s platform, blocking and callable boundaries apply.\n\n## Verbatim Yin gate output\n\nEOF\narch; date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'; git status --short --branch; rg 'PASS|current|twinned|FAIL' /private/tmp/jolt-p1c-final-matrix.log | tail -18; tail -10 /private/tmp/jolt-p1c-yin-gate.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
