{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(defmacro (defcfn|with-|cfn)|\"'^'\"\\\\(defn .*cfn|\"'^'\"\\\\(defmacro' stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj | head -35; sed -n '1600,1690p' stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj; sed -n '88,106p' host/chez/atoms.ss; rg -n 'def-var\"'! \"jolt.ffi\"'\"' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"341:(defmacro layout\n1471:(defmacro with-arena\n1482:(defmacro with-open\n1489:(defmacro with-alloc\n1497:(defmacro with-out\n1503:(defmacro with-layout\n1509:(defmacro with-c-string\n1519:(defmacro with-c-string-array\n1617:(defmacro foreign-fn [csym argtypes rettype & args]\n1635:(defmacro cfn [& args]\n1669:(defmacro pointer-fn [argtypes rettype & args]\n1751:(defmacro defcfn [name & args]\n1860:(defmacro foreign-callable [f argtypes rettype & [opt]]\n1913:(defmacro callback [arena f argtypes rettype & [opt]]\n1926:(defmacro export! [name f argtypes rettype & [opt]]\n(defn- cfn-form [csym argtypes rettype args who]\n  (let [n (count args)]\n    (cond\n      (zero? n)\n      (list 'jolt.ffi/__cfn csym argtypes rettype)\n\n      (and (= n 1) (= (first args) :blocking))\n      (list 'jolt.ffi/__cfn csym argtypes rettype :blocking)\n\n      (and (= n 1) (map? (first args)))\n      (list 'jolt.ffi/__cfn csym argtypes rettype (first args))\n\n      :else\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"jolt.ffi/\" who \": trailing option must be \"\n                           \":blocking or an options map; got \" (vec args))\n                      {:jolt/ffi-option args})))))\n\n(defmacro foreign-fn [csym argtypes rettype & args]\n  (cfn-form csym argtypes rettype args \"foreign-fn\"))\n\n;; The babashka.ffi name for the same thing. It is a MACRO here, not a function:\n;; Chez's foreign-procedure needs its argument and result types at COMPILE time,\n;; so a literal signature is the whole reason the emitted binding is a real typed\n;; call and not an interpreter. The consequences are worth naming